section5.content:
Feedback, ratings, charts, summaries, trends, and character profiles displayed on the Platform are:

• Generated from third-party service provider input and automated aggregation;
• Provided for informational and reflective purposes only;
• Not diagnostic, predictive, evaluative, or professional assessments.

ClassZ does not provide medical, psychological, psychiatric, developmental, or educational advice and does not determine a child's abilities, personality, behaviour, or future outcomes.

section6.content:
SEN-related data is:

• Provided voluntarily by parents;
• Used solely to assist centres and coaches where possible;
• Not verified, certified, or guaranteed by ClassZ.

"SEN-friendly" tags are self-declared by centres and do not constitute endorsement or assurance of suitability.

section9.content:
We may share personal data only as necessary with:

• Centres and coaches for enrolment, attendance, and class delivery;
• Payment processors for transaction processing;
• Technology service providers supporting platform operations;
• Law enforcement or regulatory authorities where required by law.

We do not sell personal data.

section10.content:
We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to:

• Fulfil the purposes stated in this Privacy Policy;
• Comply with legal, regulatory, accounting, or reporting obligations;
• Resolve disputes or enforce agreements.

Child data and account data may be deleted or anonymised upon account closure, subject to legal retention requirements.

section12.content:
Subject to the PDPO, users may:

• Request access to their personal data;
• Request correction of inaccurate data;
• Request deletion or restriction of data, where applicable.

Requests should be submitted through the Platform or customer support and may require identity verification.

section2.content:
ClassZ is a technology platform that facilitates class discovery, enrolment, payment processing, scheduling, and the organization and display of class-related information and feedback provided by third-party service providers.

Unless expressly stated otherwise, ClassZ:

• Is not a school, education centre, or training provider;
• Does not provide educational, instructional, developmental, psychological, medical, or professional services;
• Does not employ, supervise, or control centres, coaches, or other service providers.

From time to time, ClassZ may offer its own programs or services. Where ClassZ acts as a service provider, such services will be clearly identified and may be subject to separate or additional terms.

subsection1.content:
Parent accounts are intended for parents or legal guardians enrolling children into classes.

By creating a parent account, you represent and warrant that:

• You are at least 18 years old;
• You are the parent or legal guardian of each child for whom you create a profile;
• You have full authority to provide personal data relating to your child.

subsection2.content:
Parents may create multiple child profiles under one parent account. Each child may have only one profile.

Child profiles are used solely for:

• Class enrolment;
• Schedule management;
• Display of class-related feedback.

ClassZ does not create, verify, or assess child profiles and relies on information provided by parents and centres.

subsection1.content:
Each centre owner is solely responsible for:

• The accuracy of listings and schedules;
• The delivery and quality of classes;
• The conduct, qualifications, and compliance of all coaches, managers, and personnel;
• Compliance with all applicable laws, safeguarding obligations, and professional standards.

No coach, manager, or centre personnel shall be deemed an employee, agent, or representative of ClassZ.

subsection2.content:
Zing credits:
• Are platform-specific;
• Have no cash value;
• Are non-transferable;
• May be used for multiple children under the same parent account;
• Do not expire except upon account closure.

Subscription plans are billed via a connected credit card through third-party payment processors.

Unused credits are forfeited upon account closure.

If a class session is not delivered as scheduled and no approved rearrangement is recorded on the Platform:
• The session is treated as a centre-side issue;
• Parents are eligible for a full refund for that session, subject to verification.

subsection3.content:
If no approved rearrangement is recorded on the Platform and a class proceeds as scheduled:
• Standard attendance and no-show rules apply;
• A parent's failure to attend is treated as a normal absence and is not refundable, unless otherwise stated in this policy.

section8.content:
Performance feedback is provided by centres and coaches and is not guaranteed within a specific timeframe.

• Failure to provide feedback within ten (10) days does not entitle parents to a full or partial refund of the class.
• At its discretion, ClassZ may offer a partial coupon or voucher as a goodwill measure.
• Any such compensation:
  Is non-cash and non-transferable;
  Has no fixed value;
  Is determined on a case-by-case basis;
  Does not constitute an admission of fault or create a precedent.

section9.content:
ClassZ may offer "Protected Booking" benefits in specific scenarios, including:

• Centre cancellation;
• Material difference between the service provided and its description;
• Verified fraud or misconduct;
• Approved class rearrangements that parents cannot attend.

Protected Booking benefits:

• Are subject to verification and time limits;
• Do not apply to absences without valid reason;
• Do not constitute an unconditional guarantee.

section10.content:
To request a refund:

• Parents must create a support ticket through the Platform;
• Requests must be submitted within the applicable timeframe stated in this policy;
• Requests submitted outside the stated timeframe are deemed waived.

ClassZ reserves the right to request additional information to verify eligibility.
